+- `FormAppTaskActionScenarioTest` calls the real Insight task-action service.
+  Both supported principal types prove a named non-assignee receives an access
+  denial on claim and completion, with unchanged assignees, task state, active
+  task multiset, process/local variables, and task/activity/variable history.
+  The authenticated assignee claims using the existing username assignment and
+  completes all ten arms through the product service. Reassignment between the
+  permission read and mutation is rejected by the engine's optimistic locking.
+  These checks do not prove form import/submission or general reassignment.
+
+Task actions authorize assigned tasks only for their authenticated assignee.
+Unassigned tasks require a candidate user or actual candidate-group membership
+(including parent groups) before claim; completion requires assignment. Numeric
+engine identities mean Insight user IDs; other identities mean usernames.
+Candidate or participant visibility does not override another assignee. Owner,
+initiator-extension and special subtask permissions are not implemented here.
+`assignTask` still returns null and needs a separate assignment-operation change.
+
